# SentinelFlow line-ending policy.
#
# Every text blob is stored in the repo with LF. This file pins the *checkout*
# ending per script type so a fresh clone behaves identically on every OS,
# independent of the cloner's core.autocrlf setting. Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise hand out CRLF for the bash scripts
# and break `bash scripts/quickstart.sh` (a `#!/bin/bash\r` shebang and a
# trailing CR on every line make bash fail with `$'\r': command not found`).

# Bash scripts (Linux / macOS quickstart, setup-dev, doctor, smoke) MUST be LF
# on checkout -- bash reads a trailing CR as part of the command.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# PowerShell / Windows batch are Windows-native: keep CRLF for editors and the
# console. (PowerShell also tolerates LF; CRLF is simply the convention here.)
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
